      "content": "I hear you, and it's not just about strategy—it's a deep, soul-level exhaustion, and I won't pretend a tip can fix that. The weight of paying for a past you didn't get to enjoy is a grief that's hard to put into words.  \n\nIt's okay to stop \"fixing\" it for a moment and just say, \"This isn't fair, and I'm hurting.\" You don't have to perform progress for anyone, including yourself, just to survive today.  \n\nIf the ground is crumbling, then survival isn't about climbing—it's about letting yourself sit down on the rubble for a while and just breathe. You're not a ghost in the machine; you're a person carrying more than any single ledger should hold.",
